WEBVTT

00:11.160 --> 00:13.870
I love beautiful things.

00:14.950 --> 00:19.540
Beauty has supreme value, I feel.

00:20.460 --> 00:29.590
The beautiful and cruel poet

00:23.960 --> 00:27.880
You certainly are a very beautiful person.

00:27.880 --> 00:29.590
Compared to me...

00:29.590 --> 00:32.100
It's not just outward appearance.

00:32.100 --> 00:35.560
Like in sports, there are beautiful forms and such, aren't there?

00:35.560 --> 00:39.850
Behaviour, manner of speech, and the heart.

00:39.850 --> 00:42.560
I believe this world is divided into two halves.

00:43.400 --> 00:47.070
Into the beautiful and the ugly.

00:47.650 --> 00:49.360
That's a problem.

00:49.360 --> 00:53.070
I think I'd be grouped in the ugly category.

00:53.410 --> 00:55.620
What should I do?

00:57.580 --> 00:59.710
How about killing yourself?

01:03.460 --> 01:03.710
The true forms

01:05.340 --> 01:05.590
Of the things that I gazed at

01:07.170 --> 01:07.420
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

01:10.880 --> 01:11.130
Again today, time

01:12.760 --> 01:12.970
Will only construct a loneliness

01:14.550 --> 01:14.800
That seems to be torn apart, right?

01:21.980 --> 01:22.230
There are people who can't forget about

01:25.650 --> 01:25.900
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

01:29.280 --> 01:29.530
Nevertheless, recollections

01:33.030 --> 01:33.280
Visit from the future

01:36.950 --> 01:44.330
Words that turn into sighs

01:44.080 --> 01:44.330
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:47.800 --> 01:48.050
Will I flutter apart?

01:51.510 --> 01:51.760
Growing confused and disordered

01:55.180 --> 01:55.430
I want to carve

01:57.470 --> 01:57.720
These letters to you

02:02.520 --> 02:02.770
Pieces of the truth

02:04.350 --> 02:04.600
Of things that I want to tell you-

02:06.230 --> 02:06.440
I can't even send them well to you

02:09.940 --> 02:10.190
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

02:13.610 --> 02:13.860
Then can they spill into your heart?

02:17.330 --> 02:17.580
Even if the one word left behind

02:20.540 --> 02:20.790
To us who live

02:23.250 --> 02:23.500
Is to be goodbye

02:57.030 --> 02:58.620
Found you!

03:09.710 --> 03:11.460
It got away again!

03:11.460 --> 03:12.630
Chiaki.

03:12.630 --> 03:15.720
Fumika? What are you doing in a place like this?

03:15.720 --> 03:17.010
Work.

03:18.890 --> 03:23.100
Don't tell me, you're also delivering to Schrödinger?

03:27.400 --> 03:28.560
Honestly!

03:29.020 --> 03:32.980
How are we supposed to deliver a Shigofumi to a cat?

03:32.980 --> 03:36.990
They can't understand what we say,
so they won't stop when we call them.

03:36.990 --> 03:39.950
I've been pursuing it all the way here.

03:40.240 --> 03:44.410
What? You've been chasing that cat all the way from there?

03:44.700 --> 03:45.830
Something like that.

03:45.830 --> 03:48.170
That cat sure has willpower.

03:48.170 --> 03:50.420
It's two hours by train.

03:50.420 --> 03:52.960
It's 1 hour 48 minutes via the express.

03:52.960 --> 03:55.550
That the same thing as two hours!

03:55.550 --> 03:59.050
Your approximations prevent you
from getting a normal level of achievement.

03:59.050 --> 04:02.260
My delivery success rate is unsurpassed at 100% however!

04:02.260 --> 04:03.430
Kanaka.

04:03.430 --> 04:06.350
Yes, yes. I won't waste my time with idiots.

04:06.350 --> 04:08.730
Looks like you actually understand yourself a little.

04:08.730 --> 04:10.440
I'm talking about you!

04:10.440 --> 04:11.900
Who's the sender?

04:11.900 --> 04:13.940
The old lady who's the owner of the cat.

04:13.940 --> 04:16.900
The cat was taken care of by an old,
married couple with no children apparently.

04:16.900 --> 04:17.740
And yours?

04:19.320 --> 04:20.820
It's from the old man.

04:21.120 --> 04:24.620
Oh my. So both of them went at roughly the same time?

04:25.290 --> 04:26.750
Perhaps that's for the best.

04:26.750 --> 04:27.330
Huh?

04:28.160 --> 04:32.170
It's terribly cruel to leave one half behind.

04:33.000 --> 04:34.380
You remember her, don't you?

04:34.380 --> 04:38.380
She was our classmate in Year 2 of middle school, Mikawa Fumika.

04:38.380 --> 04:41.760
<i>Ah, her! Yeah, the quiet one, right?</i>

04:41.760 --> 04:45.140
<i>Who'd ever think someone like her would shoot her own father.</i>

04:45.810 --> 04:48.980
I guess the stress must have been building inside her.

04:48.980 --> 04:51.730
Then it exploded all at once.

04:51.730 --> 04:53.690
Are you talking about Kirameki's daughter?

04:54.070 --> 04:56.280
<i>She gunned down her own father, didn't she?</i>

04:56.280 --> 04:57.400
<i>Incredible, isn't it?</i>

04:57.400 --> 04:59.110
<i>Stop being stupid.</i>

04:59.110 --> 05:02.450
<i>I guess it's different being the daughter of a novelist.</i>

04:59.950 --> 05:02.450
Mikawa Kirameki Shot. Is the murderer his only daughter, Girl A (Age 13)?

05:05.030 --> 05:06.830
Why did you do it, Mikawa?

05:07.450 --> 05:10.250
Why did you shoot your own father?

05:14.250 --> 05:15.380
Mikawa...

05:15.670 --> 05:15.710
The feel-good

05:15.670 --> 05:15.710
place!!

05:18.840 --> 05:24.930
I figure it'd be too hard to look for it blindly.

05:18.970 --> 05:19.010
Kamome Road

05:25.560 --> 05:28.890
We <i>have</i> been searching blindly for the past three days though.

05:28.890 --> 05:31.560
I'm just saying we should use our heads.

05:33.060 --> 05:33.100
For victims

05:33.060 --> 05:33.100
of the disease

05:33.060 --> 05:33.100
of poor eating

05:33.060 --> 05:33.100
habits, diabetes,

05:33.060 --> 05:33.100
there's Turmeric Tea.

05:34.980 --> 05:36.020
Catnip?

05:36.020 --> 05:37.440
Ding ding!

05:37.730 --> 05:41.280
That's right! Cats love catnip.

05:41.280 --> 05:43.820
It's a method grounded in theory, but it's effective.

05:43.820 --> 05:45.030
Exactly.

05:45.530 --> 05:48.370
Matoma, 0923!

05:50.790 --> 05:52.000
What are you planning to do?

05:52.000 --> 05:53.580
It's obvious isn't it?

05:53.580 --> 05:57.380
We don't have any money from this world.

05:57.380 --> 05:58.090
Really?

05:58.090 --> 06:00.420
So, you're going to steal?

06:00.420 --> 06:01.840
I'm just borrowing.

06:01.840 --> 06:02.470
Forever...

06:04.430 --> 06:04.470
Stop!

06:04.430 --> 06:04.470
Check left

06:04.430 --> 06:04.470
and right

06:04.470 --> 06:04.510
Stop!

06:07.810 --> 06:09.390
I won't allow stealing.

06:09.390 --> 06:12.310
What choice do we have? We have no money.

06:12.850 --> 06:15.270
I can't hold back because I can't see you.

06:14.350 --> 06:16.770
Fu-Fumika! Stop swinging me!

06:15.270 --> 06:16.770
I might cause a fatal wound.

06:16.770 --> 06:19.980
You liar. You can definitely see me.

06:20.480 --> 06:21.820
Stop!

06:21.030 --> 06:22.700
Is she serious?

06:21.820 --> 06:24.610
So, how are we going to find Schrödinger?

06:24.990 --> 06:26.740
Without any money...

06:27.700 --> 06:28.740
What is it?

06:30.240 --> 06:32.120
It's very unlike you.

06:32.120 --> 06:33.580
Yeah, that's true.

06:33.580 --> 06:37.750
Normally, you'd just say that there's no recipient and run away.

06:37.750 --> 06:40.090
But, you've been chasing this cat for three days.

06:40.090 --> 06:43.010
And you're even willing to commit
robbery. Aren't you a bit extra-determined?

06:43.010 --> 06:45.260
N-Nothing wrong with being determined, right?

06:45.260 --> 06:47.470
Once in a while, even I...

06:47.470 --> 06:49.100
Hey, you girls.

06:49.890 --> 06:51.270
You two are cute.

06:51.270 --> 06:53.350
Matching uniforms?

06:53.640 --> 06:54.520
Do you know them?

06:54.520 --> 06:55.390
Not at all.

06:55.390 --> 06:57.100
Oh! Ventriloquism.

06:57.100 --> 06:58.810
You've got a great talent there!

06:58.810 --> 07:01.860
You two can definitely become very popular very quickly.

07:01.860 --> 07:03.490
So who are these people?

07:03.490 --> 07:04.570
Scouts.

07:04.570 --> 07:05.740
Scouts?

07:05.740 --> 07:07.030
Parasite.

07:07.620 --> 07:09.030
Human trash.

07:09.030 --> 07:10.280
Flea.

07:10.580 --> 07:11.870
Losing horse racing ticket.

07:12.160 --> 07:13.450
Waste of time.

07:13.450 --> 07:15.080
Photochemical smoke.

07:15.080 --> 07:16.750
A comb for a baldie.

07:16.750 --> 07:19.290
The unused plastic frame after building a model.

07:19.290 --> 07:22.630
D-Don't belittle us, you octopus!

07:25.010 --> 07:26.680
Legitimate self-defence.

07:26.680 --> 07:27.720
Hey, hold it, Fumika.

07:30.010 --> 07:34.230
Ouch! That hurts! Spare me!

07:36.520 --> 07:38.480
F-Forgive us!

07:39.060 --> 07:41.900
Please accept this as an apology.

07:44.240 --> 07:46.110
Hooray!

07:47.280 --> 07:49.280
We've got money to buy the catnip now.

07:50.200 --> 07:51.410
Say...

07:51.410 --> 07:55.330
Would you stop using me as a weapon, please?

08:00.960 --> 08:02.380
Good morning.

08:02.380 --> 08:04.010
Late morning to you.

08:05.880 --> 08:07.170
Where's Kaname?

08:07.170 --> 08:09.840
He's been on the phone in his room all morning.

08:10.180 --> 08:11.300
On the phone?

08:11.300 --> 08:14.560
I think he's talking with his friends from middle school.

08:14.560 --> 08:17.560
He was asking me where the register of names were yesterday.

08:19.270 --> 08:20.730
Middle school?

08:33.950 --> 08:36.200
Shuwa-shuwa is not coming, is it?

08:36.200 --> 08:37.540
It's Schrödinger.

08:37.540 --> 08:40.710
It sure has a long name for a cat.

08:50.550 --> 08:51.800
Say, Fumika...

08:51.800 --> 08:55.510
Tell me why you're the only one who ages.

08:57.520 --> 09:00.900
The postal workers are chosen from dead people.

09:00.900 --> 09:04.480
And we keep the form of the time we died.

09:06.230 --> 09:07.820
But, why do you...?

09:09.320 --> 09:11.820
Stop staying silent. Answer me.

09:11.820 --> 09:13.070
I...

09:26.750 --> 09:27.920
What are you doing?

09:28.260 --> 09:30.050
It's not Schrödinger.

09:30.050 --> 09:32.840
But, what's the point of chasing it away?

09:32.840 --> 09:35.430
You're gonna scare Schrödinger away too like that.

09:42.480 --> 09:43.600
Don't tell me...

09:43.900 --> 09:46.360
You're scared of cats?

09:47.440 --> 09:49.110
No, I'm not.

10:07.590 --> 10:09.210
Now, this is something.

10:17.680 --> 10:21.020
Kazuo is the younger brother and
Chionosuke is is the older brother...

10:21.020 --> 10:22.390
That's tasteful.

10:25.060 --> 10:28.070
Yes, this is Natsuka.

10:28.070 --> 10:29.440
It's Nojima.

10:29.440 --> 10:30.900
We were in the same middle school.

10:30.900 --> 10:31.360
Eh?

10:32.780 --> 10:33.820
Kaname-kun?

10:34.240 --> 10:35.530
It's been a while.

10:35.530 --> 10:38.120
Y-Yeah, it has.

10:38.120 --> 10:39.950
Why are you calling out of the blue?

10:39.950 --> 10:43.330
<i>Natsuka, do you know how to get in touch with Mikawa?</i>

10:43.330 --> 10:43.960
Huh?

10:44.250 --> 10:45.960
I need to talk to her.

10:45.960 --> 10:47.920
I'd like to know how to contact her.

10:47.920 --> 10:49.420
You were good friends with Mikawa, weren't you?

10:49.420 --> 10:50.670
<i>You were good friends with Mikawa, weren't you?</i>

10:50.670 --> 10:53.260
<i>So, I figured that you might know.</i>

10:53.260 --> 10:54.930
<i>Perhaps you have some leads.</i>

10:54.930 --> 10:56.140
Kaname-kun.

10:57.720 --> 11:00.510
Did you date Fumika?

11:01.140 --> 11:04.480
I'll tell you if you answer me honestly.

11:04.480 --> 11:05.440
I'll give you a hint.

11:05.440 --> 11:08.480
<i>A hint? Do you know something?</i>

11:08.860 --> 11:11.820
<i>You had a crush on Fumika, didn't you?</i>

11:12.650 --> 11:14.110
With Mikawa?

11:38.430 --> 11:39.800
<i>She turned me down.</i>

11:40.970 --> 11:42.390
I see.

11:42.680 --> 11:43.850
Don't tell anyone.

11:44.140 --> 11:46.810
Don't worry. Your secret is safe with me.

11:46.810 --> 11:47.900
<i>So, tell me.</i>

11:47.900 --> 11:48.520
Huh?

11:48.520 --> 11:49.610
The hint.

11:49.610 --> 11:51.480
How do I contact Mikawa?

11:51.480 --> 11:53.400
<i>Probably the hospital.</i>

11:53.400 --> 11:54.280
Hospital?

11:54.570 --> 11:57.610
I overheard the vice principal talking on the phone.

11:57.610 --> 11:59.780
Yuzawa General Hospital.

11:59.780 --> 12:01.830
He was telling someone to contact her there...

12:01.830 --> 12:04.790
because she was going to be admitted there for a while.

12:05.200 --> 12:07.330
Yuzawa General Hospital?

12:07.960 --> 12:09.290
<i>Thank you, Natsuka.</i>

12:13.000 --> 12:15.510
So, Fumika turned him down.

12:18.800 --> 12:21.800
And I thought Fumika liked him.

12:22.140 --> 12:24.140
Shigofumi

12:25.220 --> 12:27.230
Shigofumi

12:40.360 --> 12:41.820
Fumi-chan.

12:43.620 --> 12:44.990
You regained your senses?

12:46.620 --> 12:49.210
Unexpectedly, you have some cute parts to you as well.

12:49.870 --> 12:51.670
I can't believe you're scared of cats.

12:57.760 --> 12:58.840
Here.

12:59.590 --> 13:02.590
I still had some money left over after buying the catnip.

13:05.140 --> 13:06.430
It's open.

13:07.020 --> 13:09.350
Does it bother you? An indirect kiss.

13:11.770 --> 13:14.320
Nothing wrong, right? We're both girls after all.

13:22.070 --> 13:23.570
But, what are you going to do now?

13:23.570 --> 13:25.240
It never showed up.

13:25.240 --> 13:26.580
That's because...

13:26.580 --> 13:31.960
The scent of the catnip can't possibly
reach that far no matter how hard you try.

13:31.960 --> 13:35.170
Being able to cover the entire city is highly unlikely...

13:36.670 --> 13:37.800
That was...

13:37.800 --> 13:39.420
Schrödinger!

13:51.270 --> 13:52.730
Ooh, as expected of Fumika.

13:53.810 --> 13:55.980
0825!

14:15.250 --> 14:16.340
You're in the way.

14:16.790 --> 14:19.300
You too! Don't get in my way, okay?!

14:19.880 --> 14:22.090
Kanaka, 0609.

14:22.090 --> 14:23.840
That's more like it!

14:33.100 --> 14:34.140
Fumika, your front!

14:41.610 --> 14:44.240
I'm the one who's been chasing it for three days, okay?

14:44.240 --> 14:46.570
You'd better give way to Big Sister.

14:46.570 --> 14:49.870
Big Sister? You can't even age.

14:49.870 --> 14:51.620
Ah, that's right.

14:51.620 --> 14:55.540
Unlike you, I'm forever young.

14:55.540 --> 14:58.000
In other words, forever flat-chested.

14:58.290 --> 15:00.550
You're flat-chested as well!

15:00.550 --> 15:02.460
I'll have a sexy body in five years time.

15:02.460 --> 15:06.140
You won't know for sure right? There
are some adults who don't mature at all.

15:06.140 --> 15:07.340
That would be you, Chiaki.

15:07.340 --> 15:08.220
What was that?!

15:50.140 --> 15:52.930
Fumika! In front of you!

16:01.900 --> 16:04.650
Sorry, are you okay?

16:05.990 --> 16:07.280
Mikawa!

16:09.160 --> 16:10.780
What the hell was that?

16:12.410 --> 16:13.450
What's going on?

16:16.410 --> 16:19.540
Sorry, but please don't struggle.

16:19.540 --> 16:21.340
I have my reasons.

16:23.340 --> 16:25.260
What reasons?

16:25.260 --> 16:27.010
Were you climbing trees?

16:27.300 --> 16:29.090
Oh, are you running from the hospital?

16:29.090 --> 16:32.050
No, it's not that.

16:33.180 --> 16:33.970
What's going on?

16:34.260 --> 16:37.430
Sorry, I had a little accident.

16:37.430 --> 16:38.850
Stay calm, Fumika!

16:39.140 --> 16:40.850
But...

16:48.900 --> 16:50.070
Now is my chance!

16:51.110 --> 16:53.410
Is he all right?

16:53.410 --> 16:56.580
He's all right. The hospital is right in front of him.

16:56.580 --> 16:59.750
Uh... I don't think that necessarily means he's all right...

17:14.430 --> 17:15.100
Chiaki...

17:15.680 --> 17:18.060
Flight mode is about to expire.

17:18.060 --> 17:20.940
Keep it running. Just a bit more.

17:20.940 --> 17:21.730
Chiaki.

17:21.730 --> 17:22.850
Eh, Fumika?

17:23.400 --> 17:24.820
Are they demolishing the place?

17:25.110 --> 17:26.440
Let's turn back, Chiaki.

17:26.440 --> 17:28.780
No, we still can make it.

17:28.780 --> 17:29.440
Chiaki!

17:41.420 --> 17:42.540
Time's up.

17:53.760 --> 17:55.220
You're safe.

17:55.220 --> 17:57.060
Kanaka, cancel the code.

17:57.060 --> 17:58.220
0913.

17:58.220 --> 17:59.270
Got it!

18:10.240 --> 18:11.450
Get away from me!

18:11.450 --> 18:12.280
Help!

18:12.280 --> 18:13.490
It's possessed!

18:13.490 --> 18:15.030
Run for it!

18:22.250 --> 18:25.000
There, there. You're safe now.

18:27.250 --> 18:29.130
So, you like cats.

18:29.500 --> 18:33.090
I wouldn't call it "like" - it's my lucky item.

18:33.800 --> 18:36.760
Even when I got first place at the sports meet.

18:36.760 --> 18:40.220
And when Father came home early from the government office.

18:41.220 --> 18:43.770
And also, when I met him.

18:44.270 --> 18:49.230
I believed that our time together was just starting.

18:49.780 --> 18:52.240
So, that's why you want to age?

18:52.240 --> 18:53.530
Not really.

18:53.530 --> 18:55.280
I'm already dead after all.

18:55.780 --> 18:59.280
Chiaki, it looks like today is a lucky day.

18:59.280 --> 19:00.330
Why?

19:00.330 --> 19:02.790
There's going to be a mountain of
paperwork to do when we get back.

19:03.460 --> 19:05.080
You made a new friend.

19:18.140 --> 19:19.550
That room...

19:20.220 --> 19:23.480
This is where the senders used to live when they were still alive.

19:29.400 --> 19:32.190
You wanted to go back home, huh?

19:42.330 --> 19:43.790
I see!

19:43.790 --> 19:45.500
It's the key to this room.

20:11.310 --> 20:15.240
So that's why it could travel a
distance which takes two hours by train.

20:15.990 --> 20:20.910
To that old couple, the cat was their only family.

20:22.120 --> 20:25.200
I made sure that machine won't function until tomorrow morning.

20:25.830 --> 20:29.250
Take your time today to bid your farewells.

20:30.500 --> 20:33.380
Fumika, how about your family?

20:34.550 --> 20:36.260
I ended it.

20:37.670 --> 20:37.720
Mikawa Fumika

20:46.520 --> 20:47.730
Mikawa...

20:49.190 --> 20:50.560
Looks like you managed to find the place.

20:55.570 --> 20:56.780
Father?

21:12.420 --> 21:13.750
Mikawa...

21:16.880 --> 21:20.800
She has not once woken up since the incident three years ago.

21:21.090 --> 21:23.050
Never woken?

21:23.050 --> 21:24.140
Then...

21:30.310 --> 21:32.980
Who was she?

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Shigofumi

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
Episode Five

21:51.250 --> 21:56.090
I'm home

23:27.180 --> 23:29.850
A recent, yet distant incident.

23:30.560 --> 23:33.350
Is the despair of people a coincidence?

23:33.350 --> 23:34.940
Or is it inevitable?

23:36.190 --> 23:38.150
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:38.730 --> 23:39.940
Scream.

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Shigofumi

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Episode Six

23:39.230 --> 23:41.230
Scream
